{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_013qmR1yuKY4krk6gV1dWdLc", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Moreau_Gottschalk\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.classicals.de/gottschalk\"}, {\"url\": \"https://classicalm.com/en/composer/282/--\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.taminoautographs.com/blogs/autograph-blog/louis-moreau-gottschalk-the-first-great-american-composer\"}, {\"url\": \"https://sin80.com/en/artist/gottschalk\"}, {\"url\": \"https://phoenixcd.com/artist_conductor/louis-moreau-gottschalk/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://64parishes.org/?p=37116\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.bellperc.com/blogs/repertoire/louis-moreau-gottschalk\"}, {\"url\": \"https://pt.billiongraves.com/grave/Louis-Moreau-Gottschalk/5785341\"}, {\"url\": \"https://wikipedia.classicistranieri.com/en/articles/l/o/u/Louis_Moreau_Gottschalk_afc5.html\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:41:30.430Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk collapsed yellow fever performance theater Rio de Janeiro", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01LFED7fb6GapJtCNBC29RyF", "content": [{"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Moreau_Gottschalk"}, {"title": "www.classicals.de", "url": "https://www.classicals.de/gottschalk"}, {"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk", "url": "https://classicalm.com/en/composer/282/--"}, {"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk - The First Great American Composer December 24 2020", "url": "https://www.taminoautographs.com/blogs/autograph-blog/louis-moreau-gottschalk-the-first-great-american-composer"}, {"title": "sin80.com", "url": "https://sin80.com/en/artist/gottschalk"}, {"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk", "url": "https://phoenixcd.com/artist_conductor/louis-moreau-gottschalk/"}, {"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk", "url": "https://64parishes.org/?p=37116"}, {"title": "louis moreau gottschalk", "url": "https://www.bellperc.com/blogs/repertoire/louis-moreau-gottschalk"}, {"title": "pt.billiongraves.com", "url": "https://pt.billiongraves.com/grave/Louis-Moreau-Gottschalk/5785341"}, {"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk afc5", "url": "https://wikipedia.classicistranieri.com/en/articles/l/o/u/Louis_Moreau_Gottschalk_afc5.html"}]}, "Gottschalk collapsed during a concert at the Teatro Lyrico Fluminense in Rio de Janeiro on November 24, 1869, and the sources disagree on the cause. Most say yellow fever, but some say malaria.\n\n- **Collapse:** Most sources date it to November 24, 1869, at the Teatro Lyrico Fluminense. One source gives November 25 for the concert at Rio. During one of these concerts, at the Teatro Lyrico Fluminense in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, on November 24, 1869, Gottschalk collapsed from yellow fever.\n- **Last piece:** Accounts agree he had just finished *Morte!* when he fell. The actual collapse occurred just as he started to play his celebrated piece Tremolo.\n- **Cause:** Wikipedia and several other sites attribute the collapse to yellow fever. Other sources differ. One says he collapsed from having contracted malaria. Another says he had appendicitis, which led to peritonitis.\n- **Death:** He died on December 18, 1869, at his hotel in Tijuca. The sources give quinine overdose as the probable cause. One essay instead cites empyema, the result of a ruptured abscess in the abdomen.\n- **Burial:** His remains were returned to the United States in 1870 and were interred at the Green-Wood Cemetery in Brooklyn, New York."], "durationSeconds": 8.872346833, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_013qmR1yuKY4krk6gV1dWdLc", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
